<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<Version>26.1.3.37</Version>
		<FileVersion>26.1.3.37</FileVersion>
		<Authors>Don Wibier (DevExpress)</Authors>
		<Description>Abstract DX.Data.IDataStore implementation for use with EF with FluentValidation and no Mapping logic</Description>
		<Copyright>Copyright (c) 2020 Don Wibier</Copyright>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net462;net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
		<LangVersion>8.0</LangVersion>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/donwibier/DXWeb/tree/master/DX.Data.EF</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
			26.1.3.37: Bug fixes found by a new unit test suite (DX.Data.EF.Tests). Fixed: any batch of two or more items threw (the transaction was committed inside the loop) and left the first items saved; a failed insert or update left entities tracked and poisoned the DbContext; a rejected update leaked its values into later reads and saves; UpdateAsync with an empty key inserted a new row; failures always reported DataMode.Create; an empty batch returned [null]; batch results only held the last item; DeleteAsync threw on database errors (now a failed result); TransactionalExecAsync did not commit work that had already called SaveChanges; EFDatabase.Execute(transactional: false) rolled back the work's own SaveChanges. Performance: one SaveChanges and one commit per batch; batch Update/Delete load all keys in one query; updates write only changed columns; GetByKey reads without tracking. Behaviour changes: batches are all-or-nothing; entities of a failed operation are detached from the context; GetByKey no longer returns tracked instances (it does not see unsaved changes on the context); UPDATE statements contain only the changed columns.
			26.1.3.36: Added a README.md with technical documentation, now embedded in the package via PackageReadmeFile.
			26.1.3.35: Rebuilt to align with the DXWeb v26.1.3 release wave and pick up the latest DX.Data/DX.Utils dependency versions (no direct DevExpress dependency in this package).
			23.2.3.30: Data.DataStore plus Validator and Mapper have been moved and simplified into package DX.Data
			BREAKING CHANGES:
				Data base classes moved to DX.Data package
				DX.Data package refactored to use FluentValidation with simplyfied validation logic

			23.2.3.23: Upgraded to .NET8 and DX v23.2.3 Dropped support for .NETStandard!
		</PackageReleaseNotes>
		
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\DX.Data\DX.Data.csproj" />
		<ProjectReference Include="..\DX.Utils\DX.Utils.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net462'">
		<PackageReference Include="EntityFramework" Version="6.4.4" />
		<PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" Version="9.5.4" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' != 'net462'">
		<PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" Version="12.*" />		
	</ItemGroup>

	<!--<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net6.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="6.0.33" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net7.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="7.0.20" />
	</ItemGroup>-->

	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net8.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="8.*" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net9.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="9.*" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'net10.0'">
		<PackageReference Include="Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore" Version="10.*" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
